  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The supplied backbone and sampler are unspecified. The report does not establish whether the corrected baseline already uses terminal-mask examples, so the intervention's novelty and actual difference remain uncertain.",
    "Reproduction requires an endpoint distribution, minimum context length, user-versus-event sampling policy, negative-sampling rules, and loss reduction. A 50% batch probability does not imply equal supervision when baseline batches contain multiple masked targets.",
    "The experiment lacks a budgeted baseline comparison, explicit checkpoint-selection rules, and protection against repeated validation tuning. Diagnostic branch provenance and fresh-process checkpoint/predictor parity remain unspecified.",
    "Originality 3 is plausible, but potential 7 is speculative without validation evidence. Difficulty 3 may underestimate sampler integration, diagnostic adaptation, and parity verification."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Establish prior art and determine what baseline behavior must be documented before claiming a distinct intervention.",
      "query": "Does original BERT4Rec training already include terminal-item masking or next-item fine-tuning? Compare the BERT4Rec paper and public implementations with mixed random Cloze and randomly truncated prefix terminal-mask training, identifying the sampler details needed to establish an actual baseline difference."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve implementation choices that could change the effective objective or introduce sampling shortcuts.",
      "query": "For one BERT4Rec network mixing random masked-item batches with single terminal-mask prefix batches at probability 0.5, how do per-target versus per-sequence loss normalization, uniform-user versus uniform-endpoint sampling, minimum prefix length, and negative sampling affect objective weighting and popularity or sequence-length bias? Find explicit formulations and reproducible implementation examples."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Define a credible comparison and integrity protocol within the fixed evaluation and compute constraints.",
      "query": "What established protocols support a compute-limited BERT4Rec objective ablation with training seed 42, four-category macro validation HR@10, 200 users and 99 fixed negatives per category? Address unequal supervised-target counts, checkpoint selection, paired user-bootstrap uncertainty, adaptive validation overfitting, and saved-checkpoint versus deployed-predictor parity without using test labels or combining predictors."
    }
  ]
}
